id: searx-coverage-governance
title: Establish non-regressing coverage policy
description: Turn the existing coverage report into an enforceable quality gate at a realistic baseline.
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: ci,coverage,quality,tests
created_at: "2026-07-16T17:12:22.553Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-21T22:32:09.388Z"
deadline: "2026-07-19T17:12:22.553Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-16T17:14:13.666Z"
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: Coverage execution fails below documented global branch/function/line/statement floors and passes at the current repository baseline
definition_of_ready: Current full-unit coverage report is available.
parent: searx-repository-audit
reviewer: repository-owner
risk: medium
confidence: 95
sprint: 2026-07-recovery
release: next
resolution: "Configured 70% statements, 58% branches, 82% functions, and 72% lines as global Vitest coverage floors."
expected_result: The coverage command fails on material regression while current tests remain green.
actual_result: All 619 unit tests pass with observed coverage above every configured floor.
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-16T17:12:22.553Z",codex-root,The audit found coverage reporters configured without thresholds.
  "2026-07-16T17:13:44.023Z",codex-root,"Current enforced baseline passes at 72.45% statements, 60.77% branches, 84.47% functions, and 74.45% lines."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-16T17:12:22.553Z",codex-root,"Use deliberately conservative floors so this recovery does not pretend the current 2,660-line command module is already well covered."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-16T17:12:22.553Z",codex-root,"A generated coverage report is observability, not a regression gate, until thresholds are configured."
  "2026-07-16T17:13:44.023Z",codex-root,A two-point margin below observed coverage avoids flaky rounding while still preventing material regression.
files[1]{path,scope,note}:
  vitest.config.ts,project,Coverage policy
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  "bun run test:coverage",project,180
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  CONTRIBUTING.md,project,Contributor verification guidance
close_reason: "Global coverage floors are configured, documented, and pass against all 619 unit tests."
body: "The repository collects V8 coverage but configures no minimum thresholds, so meaningful regressions can remain green. Capture the post-upgrade baseline, establish conservative global floors below current results, and keep the richer HTML/LCOV artifacts available for future ratchets."
